{"content":[{"c":["GEMATRIA*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["One of the rabbinic hermeneutic rules for interpreting the OT. It consisted of explaining a word or group of words according to the numerical value of the letters or by substituting and rearranging certain letters according to a set system. By that rule of interpretation, for example, some rabbis have argued that Eliezer (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.15.2","r":"Gen.15.2","rawR":"Gen.15.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.15.2","value":"Gen.15.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 15:2"},") was worth all the servants of Abraham put together, for Abraham had 318 servants and Eliezer’s name equaled 318 (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.14.14","r":"Gen.14.14","rawR":"Gen.14.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.14.14","value":"Gen.14.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 14:14"},"). The name Babylon is arrived at in ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.25.26","r":"Jer.25.26","rawR":"Jer.25.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.25.26","value":"Jer.25.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jeremiah 25:26"}," and ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.51.41","r":"Jer.51.41","rawR":"Jer.51.41","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.51.41","value":"Jer.51.41"}],"t":"ref","v":"51:41"}," by substituting the last letter of the Hebrew word for the first letter of the same word."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["The pseudepigraphal Epistle of Barnabas interprets the 318 servants of Abraham (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.14.14","r":"Gen.14.14","rawR":"Gen.14.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.14.14","value":"Gen.14.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 14:14"},") as pointing to Jesus’ death on the cross, because 300 is the numerical value of the Greek letter “t,” which is cross-shaped, and 18 the value of the first two letters of the Greek word for Jesus. In the book of Revelation the number of the beast is 666 (",{"href":"?bref=Rev.13.18","r":"Rev.13.18","rawR":"Rev.13.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.13.18","value":"Rev.13.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"Rv 13:18"},"). If the number seven is considered to be the perfect number in the Bible, and if three sevens represent complete perfection, then the number 666 falls completely short of perfection."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Gematria","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 15:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.15.2","rawQueryValue":"Gen.15.2","sourceRefExact":"Gen.15.2"},{"anchorText":"Gn 14:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.14.14","rawQueryValue":"Gen.14.14","sourceRefExact":"Gen.14.14"},{"anchorText":"Jeremiah 25:26","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.25.26","rawQueryValue":"Jer.25.26","sourceRefExact":"Jer.25.26"},{"anchorText":"51:41","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.51.41","rawQueryValue":"Jer.51.41","sourceRefExact":"Jer.51.41"},{"anchorText":"Gn 14:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.14.14","rawQueryValue":"Gen.14.14","sourceRefExact":"Gen.14.14"},{"anchorText":"Rv 13:18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Rev.13.18","rawQueryValue":"Rev.13.18","sourceRefExact":"Rev.13.18"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"8b7eb3fbcaa97b9772cd101d1dca4ae82e1798b3e2100508cabf0cdbd77b0da4","sourceItemName":"Gematria","sourceItemOrder":86,"sourceMember":"Articles/G.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Gematria","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Gematria*","title":"Gematria*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}